==========================================
DAY 17 NOTES — Cron Jobs & Task Scheduling
Date: 15-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- Cron syntax: minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week (5 fields)
- * = every, , = list, - = range, / = step
- crontab -e edits MY personal schedule; crontab -l lists it; crontab -r deletes it all
- Shortcuts: @reboot, @daily, @hourly, @weekly save typing common patterns
- Cron runs with a MINIMAL environment — always use FULL paths in commands
- Always redirect output (>> log 2>&1) or failures happen silently, unnoticed

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] crontab -e / crontab -l / crontab -r
[ ] writing a basic */1 test cron job
[ ] writing a @daily or 0 6 * * * schedule
[ ] combining day-of-week ranges (1-5 for weekdays)

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ crontab -e (test job added)
> 

$ cat cron_test.log (after waiting a few minutes)
> 


